lines=['# G2 prefix-record compatibility and memory qualification','','The exact native libraries from the passed [SDK comparison](../2026-10-25-g2-prefix-sdk/README.md) pass compatibility, concurrency, stack and resource qualification. No native prover code is rebuilt. The qualification adds197 internally verified SDK calls and four large proofs, with75 distinct Gnark-verified exports and150 proof/public files. This phase is not a new latency comparison.','','Portable x86-64 builds disable IFMA and assembly and pass11 field,89 core, two raw-format and six cubic tests. Eight real Euler/raw OFF/ON processes verify32 SDK calls. The G2 native trace is absent on the portable path. Native compatibility adds raw/preparation-denied and single-worker proofs; primary and merge54 also pass with512KiB and1MiB worker stacks in both modes. Across these functional checks:96 SDK calls,24 independently verified exports. This is not physical ARM/Wasm/phone qualification.','','Four32-worker concurrent-caller cases run four callers and two rounds on primary and merge54 with both modes. Mutable SDKs share an immutable mapped key and existing global pool. All32 fresh proofs independently verify, and thread receipts check the pool plus actual callers.','','Nine warm pressure cases compare accepted, identical OFF and ON at32 workers with default/retained allocator policies and retained96-worker controls. Each warms at512MiB, then explicitly touches32MiB of controller ballast and lowers the group to128MiB soft/192MiB hard with swap0 before two further proofs. All cases pass without max/OOM/kill events or timeout. They cover45 SDK calls and nine exports.','','| Warm case | Variant | Whole-cgroup peak MiB, including ballast |','| --- | --- | ---: |']
